    "details": "# Problem Description:\n\nBy default, jailed processes cannot mount filesystems, including\nnullfs(4). However, the allow.mount.nullfs option enables mounting\nnullfs filesystems, subject to privilege checks.\n\nIf a privileged user within a jail is able to nullfs-mount directories,\na limitation of the kernel\\'s path lookup logic allows that user to\nescape the jail\\'s chroot, yielding access to the full filesystem of the\nhost or parent jail.\n\n# Impact:\n\nIn a jail configured to allow nullfs(4) mounts from within the jail, the\njailed root user can escape the jail\\'s filesystem root.\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0022",
